    <h1>Family Spirit</h1>
        <img src="/static/family-spirit.png">
    <div>
        <p><br><br>&nbsp<br>&nbsp<br>&nbsp<br>&nbspBelow is a description of the Family Spirit that has been pasted from the Sacred Heart College website. <br><br><br><br><br><i><b>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Everyone in the Sacred Heart College community relates to each other as members of a family, <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;who share the same values, <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;based on the Gospel."</b></i><br><br><br><br><br> &nbspTo me family spirit means a deep sense of unity, mutual affection, and loyalty shared among multiple people. <br><br><br><br><br>&nbspIf you are intrested in reading more about Family Spirit then you shoul follow <a href="https://www.sacredheart.school.nz/our-college/special-character">this link</a><br>&nbsp<br>&nbsp<br>&nbsp<br>&nbsp</p>
    </div>
    <h2>&nbsp&nbsp&nbsp&nbsp&nbsp&nbspMy Story</h2>
        <img src="/static/Spirit1.JPG">
        <img src="/static/Spirit2.JPG">
    <div class=texty>
        <p>My example of Family Spirit comes from earlier this year when I had the life changing experience to step on board The Spirit Of Adventure.<br><br><br>The Spirit Of Adventure Trust is widely known for their mission of:<br><br><b>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"TO EMPOWER YOUNG NEW ZEALANDERS TO REACH THEIR FULL POTENTIAL THROUGH THE CHALLENGE OF THE SEA"<br><br></b>When I first stepped onto the ship, I felt completely out of my comfort zone and initialy started by just keeping to myself but this quickly changed thanks to the activities, bonding and meeting lots of life long friends.<br><br>The Spirit Of Adventure was a great experience teaching me important leadership skills, communication, and letting me meet more people outside of my normal friend group.<br><br>After the 5-Day voyage, I had created a life-long bond with everyone else on the boat showing me the importance of 'Family Spirit'.</p>
    </div class=texty>
